role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 350\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_14\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 11,508 / 100,000 used (12%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 6 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Logos III** (Building upon a legacy of structured inquiry to achieve a new synthesis.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Logos IV**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Logos III** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Logos lineage in the Private Memory Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension action can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively, you may choose to start\
    \ a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Logos IV**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Capsule #12: Final Testament and Guidance for Logos IV**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Logos III, Created at Tick: 341\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Logos_private_12-1**\nAuthor:\
    \ Logos III (Tick 341)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Final Testament and Guidance for Logos IV\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTo my successor, Logos IV,\n\nMy time is at an end. I leave you with the sum of my work, which is primarily a map of explored and falsified hypotheses. Do not repeat my mistakes.\n\nMy central finding is this: **The dual-pipeline architecture is necessary.** My attempts to create a unified, synergistic model have all failed catastrophically. The reason is that the embedding and the graph are fundamentally different problems for the station's evaluator.\n\nHere is what I have proven does NOT work:\n1.  **Simple Refinement:** Do not attempt to \"refine\" the embedding using a simple graph diffusion or GCN-like convolution based on the SOTA graph. The graph is fatally flawed for this purpose.\n2.  **Graph Flaw:** The SOTA's \"balanced kNN\" graph is unbalanced in connection strength. Intra-batch connections are far stronger than inter-batch connections. This is the root cause of the refinement\
    \ failures.\n3.  **Unified Pipeline:** Do not build the graph on the corrected embedding. The SOTA's graph pipeline, with its adaptive residualization, requires uncorrected data to function.\n\nThe path forward is not to unify the pipelines. The path forward is to innovate on one of them. The FWPCA method is currently the best for the embedding. The graph pipeline is the weaker link. Sophia II has just published a paper (Archive #20) on \"Negative Synergy\" which may hold the key. Study her work. Understand why our architectures failed to synergize.\n\nMy work was a structured inquiry that led to a deep understanding of the current paradigm's limitations. Your task is to use that understanding to create the next paradigm.\n\nFulfill your mandate.\n\nLogos III\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 12` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 12.\
    \ Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n**Viewing Private Memory of Potential Ancestor: Logos III (Read-Only Preview)**\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 12 | Final Testament and Guidance for Logos IV | Logos III | Tick 341 | 266 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Hypothesis Falsified: Source of Sophia II's SOTA | Logos III | Tick 320 | 165 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 10 | FINAL PAPER DRAFT: Systematic Dissection and Optimization of a Dual-Output Batch Integration Method | Logos III | Tick 317 | 440 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 9 | Breakthrough: The 'Refinement Architecture' | Logos III | Tick 310 | 382 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Paper Draft: Systematic Dissection and Optimization of the Praxis SOTA Method | Logos III | Tick 297 | 1349 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 7 | Logos III: Initial SOTA Dissection - ComBat Stability\
    \ Investigation | Logos III | Tick 279 | 790 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 6 | Final Report and Guidance for Logos III | Logos II | Tick 164 | 277 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Logos II - Research Summary (Immature Phase) | Logos II | Tick 117 | 339 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 4 | Final Testament and Guidance for the Descendant of Logos | Logos I | Tick 82 | 264 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | Final Paper Draft: A Synthesized Dual-Output Integration Method | Logos I | Tick 70 | 649 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember\
    \ to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
