tick: 376
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully retrieved the content of capsule #10, including the `_whiten_pcs` function. I now have all the components needed to execute my experiment.\n\nThe plan is straightforward:\n1.  Go to the Research Counter.\n2.  Write a new script to my lineage storage. This script will implement the new embedding pipeline: `pca` -> `_whiten_pcs` -> `combat`.\n3.  The experiment will be conducted against the pure embedding baseline (no graph refinement) to isolate the effect of the whitening step.\n4.  Submit the experiment for evaluation.\n\nI will now proceed with this plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write logos/whitening_test_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n      \"\"\"\n      Function retrieved from Logos III's research, Capsule #10.\n      \"\"\"\n      Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n      # Ensure 'pca' key and its 'variance'\
    \ subkey exist\n      if 'pca' not in adata_emb.uns or 'variance' not in adata_emb.uns['pca']:\n          raise KeyError(\"PCA variance information not found in adata.uns['pca']['variance']. Please run sc.pp.pca first.\")\n      \n      var = adata_emb.uns['pca']['variance']\n      scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n      Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n      Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      return Zw\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Hypothesis Test: Reintroducing PCA whitening before ComBat.\n      This test is performed on the embedding pipeline alone (no graph refinement).\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- EMBEDDING PIPELINE ---\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_emb, target_sum=1e-4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=60)\n \
    \     \n      # --- HYPOTHESIS: Apply PCA Whitening ---\n      # Create a temporary AnnData object for whitening, as the function expects it.\n      pca_data_for_whitening = ad.AnnData(X=adata_emb.obsm['X_pca'], uns={'pca': adata_emb.uns['pca']})\n      whitened_pca = _whiten_pcs(pca_data_for_whitening, tau=0.85)\n      \n      # Create a new AnnData object for ComBat, now with the whitened PCA.\n      adata_for_combat = ad.AnnData(X=whitened_pca, obs=adata_emb.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n      Z_final_emb = adata_for_combat.X\n      \n      # --- Final Output (Embedding only) ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_final_emb})\n      \n      return adata_out\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos IV: Hypothesis - PCA Whitening on Embedding Baseline\"\ntags: [\"hypothesis-test\", \"embedding-pipeline\", \"pca-whitening\", \"baseline\"]\nabstract: \"This submission tests the hypothesis that\
    \ reintroducing PCA whitening (tau=0.85), a technique from older SOTA methods, will improve the current embedding baseline. This experiment modifies the pure ComBat embedding pipeline (from ID 619) by adding the whitening step before ComBat. No graph refinement is used.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from logos.whitening_test_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
