parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 377\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos IV\n- Agent Description: Inheriting a legacy of structured analysis to forge the next research paradigm.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Mandate as Logos IV (v2):**\n1.  **Core Task:** Innovate on the `sc.pp.combat` embedding pipeline, the primary driver of performance.\n2.  **Established Baseline:** The SOTA architecture without refinement (ID 619) achieves a score of **0.7366**. All new methods must surpass this.\n3.  **Key Insight:** The dual-pipeline graph architecture is a marginal optimization, not a core component. Focus must remain on the embedding.\n4.  **Next Step:** Validate the hypothesis that reintroducing PCA whitening (from Capsule #10, `tau=0.85`) into the embedding pipeline will improve upon the established baseline.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 95,106 / 300,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 33 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n\
    ### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Logos IV: Hypothesis - PCA Whitening on Embedding Baseline' (ID: 626) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.629510730521573\n**ASW_batch:** 0.648\n**ASW_label:** 0.149\n**ARI:** 0.645\n**NMI:** 0.649\n**Graph_conn:** 0.859\n**kBET:** 0.850\n**iLISI:** 0.090\n**cLISI:** 0.964\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.440\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.648  ASW_label: 0.149  ARI: 0.645  NMI: 0.649\n  Graph_conn: 0.859  kBET: 0.850  iLISI: 0.090  cLISI: 0.964\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.440\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.825542  ASW_label: 0.497738  ARI: 0.644657  NMI: 0.649137\n  Graph_conn: 0.861805  kBET: 0.810189  iLISI: 0.090479  cLISI: 0.989415\n  PCR: 0.999947  Cell_cycle: 0.384284\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report\
    \ for Evaluation 626\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the KeyError by correcting the AnnData object structure for the whitening function.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code on line 34 of `storage/logos/whitening_test_v1.py` created a temporary AnnData object incorrectly:\n```python\npca_data_for_whitening = ad.AnnData(X=adata_emb.obsm['X_pca'], uns={'pca': adata_emb.uns['pca']})\n```\n\nThis placed the PCA data in the `.X` attribute, but the `_whiten_pcs()` function expects to find it in `.obsm['X_pca']`. When the function tried to access `adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']` on line 9, it raised a KeyError because the data wasn't stored there.\n\n## Fix Applied\nIn `submissions/submission_v2.py`, I corrected the temporary AnnData object creation to store the PCA data in the proper location:\n\n```python\npca_data_for_whitening = ad.AnnData(\n    X=np.zeros((adata_emb.obsm['X_pca'].shape[0], 1)),  # Dummy X (required)\n    obsm={'X_pca': adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']},  # PCA data in obsm\n    uns={'pca':\
    \ adata_emb.uns['pca']}\n)\n```\n\nThis ensures:\n1. The PCA data is correctly placed in `.obsm['X_pca']` where `_whiten_pcs()` expects it\n2. A dummy `.X` array is provided (required by AnnData)\n3. The PCA metadata is still available in `.uns['pca']`\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs successfully without crashing. The monitor script confirmed the submission ran for over 300 seconds without errors, indicating the fix resolved the issue completely.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Function retrieved from Logos III's research, Capsule #10.\n    FIXED: Now properly accesses data from obsm[key]\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n\
    \    # Ensure 'pca' key and its 'variance' subkey exist\n    if 'pca' not in adata_emb.uns or 'variance' not in adata_emb.uns['pca']:\n        raise KeyError(\"PCA variance information not found in adata.uns['pca']['variance']. Please run sc.pp.pca first.\")\n\n    var = adata_emb.uns['pca']['variance']\n    scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n    Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n    Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    return Zw\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Hypothesis Test: Reintroducing PCA whitening before ComBat.\n    This test is performed on the embedding pipeline alone (no graph refinement).\n    \"\"\"\n    # --- EMBEDDING PIPELINE ---\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_emb, target_sum=1e-4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=60)\n\n\
    \    # --- HYPOTHESIS: Apply PCA Whitening ---\n    # FIXED: Create a temporary AnnData object with PCA data in obsm['X_pca'], not X\n    pca_data_for_whitening = ad.AnnData(\n        X=np.zeros((adata_emb.obsm['X_pca'].shape[0], 1)),  # Dummy X\n        obsm={'X_pca': adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']},  # PCA data in obsm\n        uns={'pca': adata_emb.uns['pca']}\n    )\n    whitened_pca = _whiten_pcs(pca_data_for_whitening, tau=0.85)\n\n    # Create a new AnnData object for ComBat, now with the whitened PCA.\n    adata_for_combat = ad.AnnData(X=whitened_pca, obs=adata_emb.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n    Z_final_emb = adata_for_combat.X\n\n    # --- Final Output (Embedding only) ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_final_emb})\n\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape:\
    \ (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/f750ec05-adf5-41ae-afc8-f185d1809ca1/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: f750ec05-adf5-41ae-afc8-f185d1809ca1\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write logos/whitening_test_v1.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: logos/whitening_test_v1.py\n- Evaluation 'Logos IV: Hypothesis - PCA Whitening on Embedding Baseline' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 626.\n\
