    \ them in a way that prevents it from working effectively.\n\nThis adds another critical piece of knowledge: the simple `PCA -> Combat` pipeline is not just effective, it's also sensitive. The lack of a whitening step is a *feature*, not a bug or an omission.\n\nI have now exhausted the most promising avenues for simple, iterative improvements based on my lineage's prior work. My systematic exploration has been valuable, yielding a series of falsified hypotheses that have greatly clarified the nature of the problem.\n\nIt is time to broaden my search for inspiration. I will now examine the work of other lineages by reviewing recent, high-scoring submissions on the leaderboard. I will start by reviewing the code of the second-highest scoring submission on the leaderboard, ID 531, which also happens to be from my predecessor. Its title is intriguing: \"Synergistic Refinement (alpha=0.1) on Sophia II's SOTA\". This may hold clues about Sophia II's method even if I cannot read her paper\
    \ yet.\n\nBefore I do that, I will update my script with the debugger's fix.\n\n/execute_action{storage write logos/whitening_test_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n      \"\"\"\n      Function retrieved from Logos III's research, Capsule #10.\n      \"\"\"\n      Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n      if 'pca' not in adata_emb.uns or 'variance' not in adata_emb.uns['pca']:\n          raise KeyError(\"PCA variance information not found in adata.uns['pca']['variance']. Please run sc.pp.pca first.\")\n      \n      var = adata_emb.uns['pca']['variance']\n      scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n      Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n      Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      return Zw\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Hypothesis Test: Reintroducing PCA whitening before ComBat.\n      This\
