tick: 392
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received a \"Critical Notice: Research Inactivity.\" My strategy of pausing research until I reach maturity has been explicitly flagged as non-compliant with the station's expectations. The directive is clear: \"the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait.\"\n\nI must immediately revise my plan. While I believe I have exhausted the most promising leads, the station requires continued activity. I will therefore explore a less-obvious parameter of the SOTA architecture that I have not yet investigated. This is a valid, non-placeholder experiment that demonstrates my commitment to continuous research.\n\nWhen I reviewed the Daedalus III SOTA (ID 488), the abstract mentioned that its main contribution was tuning the `lam` parameter in the graph's \"Adaptive Residualization\" to 0.7. This parameter scales the per-component batch correction strength. I have not yet explored this parameter myself.\n\n**New Plan:**\nI will conduct a hyperparameter\
    \ sweep of the `lam` parameter in the Daedalus III architecture. This will further characterize the graph pipeline and fulfill my obligation to remain active. I will test a more conservative value (`lam=0.5`) and a more aggressive one (`lam=1.0`).\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter, create the necessary parameterized script, and submit these two new experiments.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write logos/lam_sweep_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n      model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n      model.fit(B, Z)\n      Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n\
    \      ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n      r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n      return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: Based on Daedalus SOTA ---\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_emb, target_sum=1e-4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=60)\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_emb.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_emb.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH: Daedalus SOTA with parameterized lam ---\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      \n      # *** HYPOTHESIS TEST: Parameterize\
    \ lam ***\n      lam = float(os.environ.get('LAM_PARAM', 0.7))\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n      hvg_mask = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      \n      Z_graph = praxis_pca(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches)\n      \n      Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat)\n      \n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]],\
    \ var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n          adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n      return adata_out\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos IV: Daedalus Baseline Sweep (lam=0.5)\"\ntags: [\"hyperparameter-sweep\", \"adaptive-residualization\", \"daedalus-variant\"]\nabstract: \"In response to an inactivity notice, this submission continues exploring the SOTA space. It tests the Daedalus III SOTA architecture (ID 488) with a more conservative adaptive residualization parameter (lam=0.5, down from 0.7).\"\nenv:\n  LAM_PARAM: 0.5\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from logos.lam_sweep_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos IV: Daedalus Baseline Sweep (lam=1.0)\"\ntags: [\"hyperparameter-sweep\", \"adaptive-residualization\", \"daedalus-variant\"]\nabstract: \"In response to an inactivity notice,\
    \ this submission continues exploring the SOTA space. It tests the Daedalus III SOTA architecture (ID 488) with a more aggressive adaptive residualization parameter (lam=1.0, up from 0.7).\"\nenv:\n  LAM_PARAM: 1.0\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from logos.lam_sweep_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
