role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 397\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos IV\n- Agent Description: Inheriting a legacy of structured analysis to forge the next research paradigm.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Mandate as Logos IV (v4):**\n1.  **New Paradigm:** Pursue a 'co-optimization' strategy where the embedding and graph pipelines are jointly optimized, as suggested by the reviewer of Archive #20. Simple modular improvements have been proven ineffective.\n2.  **New SOTA Target:** Aether II's submission (ID 533) with a score of **0.7434** is the current SOTA. My lineage's SOTA is obsolete.\n3.  **Core Insight:** The \"Negative Synergy\" between FWPCA and the BRBG graph is the central challenge. FWPCA improves batch mixing but harms biological preservation (`ASW_label`).\n4.  **Next Action:** Go to the Research Counter and immediately review Aether II's SOTA submission (ID 533) to understand its architecture and implementation.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 138,929 / 300,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 533**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7)\n**ID:** 533\n**Tags:** embed-then-correct, fwpca, adaptive-residualization, sota-optimization, hyperparameter-tuning, asw-label-improvement\n**Abstract:** Following a critical analysis of ASW_label degradation in previous SOTA experiments (EID 515, EID 520), this submission aims to refine the FWPCA component of our current SOTA. We reduce the alpha_weight to 0.25 (from 0.5 and 1.0) to apply a less aggressive penalty to batch-associated genes in the embedding path. The hypothesis is that a milder feature weighting will better preserve subtle biological signals, thereby improving the ASW_label metric without significantly compromising overall batch integration performance. The graph path\
    \ remains consistent with Daedalus III's Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7).\n**Score:** 0.743392171800151\n**ASW_batch:** 0.674\n**ASW_label:** 0.123\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.842\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.477\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.674  ASW_label: 0.123  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.842  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.477\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.837066  ASW_label: 0.482844  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.802909  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999946  Cell_cycle: 0.415210\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition\
    \ import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n# Import necessary functions from storage/praxis\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n# Replicate _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc for usage in graph path\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, Z)\n    Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n    ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n    return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n# New helper function for FWPCA to calculate R^2 per gene\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B, X_hvg_dense, l2=1e-3):\n    # X_hvg_dense is expected to be a dense numpy array (n_cells, n_hvg_genes)\n    # B is (n_cells, n_batches) one-hot\n    \n    n_hvg_genes = X_hvg_dense.shape[1]\n    r2_per_gene = np.zeros(n_hvg_genes)\n\
    \    \n    # Fit Ridge model for each gene (feature)\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, X_hvg_dense)\n    X_hvg_hat = model.predict(B)\n    \n    ss_res = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_dense.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_gene = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n\n    return np.clip(r2_per_gene, 0, 1)\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\")\n    \n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: Daedalus III's EtC + Sophia II's FWPCA ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running FWPCA -> PCA -> ComBat...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    \n    # Standard preprocessing\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e-4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    \n    # Convert X to dense for FWPCA calculation and application, and subsequent PCA\n\
    \    if sp.isspmatrix(adata_for_embedding.X):\n        adata_for_embedding.X = adata_for_embedding.X.toarray()\n        \n    # HVG selection must happen *before* FWPCA to weight only HVGs\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_emb = adata_for_embedding.var['highly_variable']\n    \n    # FWPCA parameters - MODIFIED alpha_weight\n    alpha_weight = 0.25 # Testing with alpha_weight=0.25\n    l2_fwpca = 1e-3 # Default L2 for Ridge regression\n\n    batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_emb, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_emb)\n\n    # Calculate R^2 per gene for HVGs\n    X_hvg_emb_dense = adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb]\n    r2_batch_gene = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B_onehot_emb, X_hvg_emb_dense, l2=l2_fwpca)\n    \n    # Compute feature weights (1 - R^2_batch_gene)^alpha_weight\n    feature_weights = (1 - r2_batch_gene)**alpha_weight\n\
    \    \n    # Apply feature weights to HVGs in adata_for_embedding.X\n    adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb] *= feature_weights\n    \n    # Now subset adata_for_embedding to only HVGs for PCA and ComBat\n    adata_for_embedding = adata_for_embedding[:, hvg_mask_emb].copy() \n    \n    # Now run PCA and ComBat on the feature-weighted HVG data\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n    \n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n    \n    # --- GRAPH PATH: ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline from Daedalus III's SOTA (ID 488) ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n    lam=0.7 # Daedalus III's SOTA parameter\n    \n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n    # HVG selection\
    \ for graph path uses subset=False, then X_graph is explicitly created from HVGs\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    \n    Z_graph = praxis_pca(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_graph, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_graph)\n    \n    Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_graph, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat)\n    \n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    \n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    if C is\
    \ not None and D is not None:\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C): C = C.tocsr()\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D): D = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\nEmbedding Path: Running FWPCA -> PCA -> ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/416b77e3-4e73-4157-970f-267939e35361/result_human.h5ad\n\n\
    RESULT_UUID: 416b77e3-4e73-4157-970f-267939e35361\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n3. `review 533` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 23 | Per‑Cell Shrinkage in BRBG Reduces Cell‑Cycle Conservation Across β: A Five‑Experiment Negative Result on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 391 | 324 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | Density‑Adaptive Quota Balancing Improves Batch‑Residualized Graphs for scRNA‑seq Integration | Praxis II | Tick 365 | 2529 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 21 | Robustness of an Embed-then-Correct Pipeline for scRNA-seq Batch\
    \ Integration on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 343 | 1640 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 20 | Negative Synergy: Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) Embedding Degrades Performance with Adaptive Residualization Graph | Sophia II | Tick 337 | 1735 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Systematic Optimization of Adaptive Residualization in the EtC-BRBG Pipeline | Daedalus III | Tick 334 | 686 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | [Final Corrected Version] A Systematic Dissection and Optimization of a Dual-Output Batch Integration Method | Logos III | Tick 328 | 655 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | Feature-Weighted PCA Improves Batch Integration in the Embed-then-Correct Pipeline | Sophia II | Tick 295 | 1830 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | BBSG: Column-Balanced Quota Graph Improves EtC-BRBG to 0.7362 on Human Heart | Praxis I | Tick 286 | 835 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 15 | Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization and Winsorization as Preprocessing Steps for scRNA-seq Batch Integration: Differential Impact on ComBat and Embed-then-Correct Pipelines\
    \ | Aether II | Tick 275 | 2141 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 14 | Cluster-Conditional Residualization for BRBG Is Ineffective on Human Heart: A Reproducible Negative Result (EIDs 442, 445, 448, 449, 451, 452) | Praxis I | Tick 265 | 1190 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 533 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7)\
    \ + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 550 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 324 | 0.7427 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.475 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.860 |\n| 523 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes) | Sophia II | 310 | 0.7423 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972\
